body='''\n\\subsection{New Benchmark: Frozen Policies on Biomedical Lectures}\nThe additional evaluation uses all160 official English questions, not translated\nreplicas. Its protocol was fixed before method outcomes: official revision,\nquery IDs, reference, checkpoints, cost vectors, fixed random allocation, metrics,\nseeds, and paired analysis were bound by hashes. Three semantic near-question\npairs were conservatively grouped, retaining all160 observations. Source-level\nsensitivity uses27 lectures. Exact image overlap against11,609 allowed old\ncorpus pages was zero;62 perceptual candidates were visually reviewed as layout\ncollisions. Empty-text embeddings explain4,720 textual screening candidates.\nThese checks support nonuse in MDRouter selection, not complete independence\nfrom every visual-model pretraining source, which remains unknown. Public slides\nthat remove copyrighted illustrations and20 empty-OCR pages are retained.\n\n'''+ '\n'.join(tab)+'\n'+biofig+'\n'+f'''FullV obtains mean nDCG{f(by['Full-Visual'],'nDCG10'):.4f}. R100 has mean positive\nregret{f(by['BM25-R100'],'mean_r'):.4f}, compared with much smaller values on the\nrepeatedly exposed Dev workloads. The transferred Q and QP policies have\nmean regrets{f(by['Q_regret'],'mean_r'):.4f} and{f(by['QP_regret'],'mean_r'):.4f}; their\nobserved means do not meet .05. This is not a formal certification failure test:\nno new certificate was issued. Query/probe information can change the quality\npoint without establishing a same-risk cost advantage.\n\n'''+ '; '.join(matched_text)+'. These envelope comparisons are retrospective descriptive analyses fitted to benchmark outcomes, not deployed mixtures or new tuning choices. Both query-family and source-cluster intervals are archived. No Biomedical outcome changes the checkpoints, thresholds, actions, or random seed.\n\n'+'''The adapted hard/soft controls now have newly measured complete paths on this\nbenchmark. Their encoder, loss and action space still differ from original\nRetrievalRouter; they must not be relabeled as a faithful reproduction.\n\n\\subsection{Additional Retriever: Actual ColPali Execution}\nThe frozen24-query pilot first detected an implementation error: zero-clipping\nnegative per-token maxima changed a sample score by up to .032753. The fix\nmasks padding and retains negative contributions; the1e-3 agreement threshold\nwas not relaxed. New attempts retained all failures and verified all254 trained\nadapter tensors. The corrected pilot passed before expansion. Historical005\nprotocols and outputs were preserved. ColPali uses its own reference; old\nmodel-specific risk predictions and certificates are not copied.\n\n'''+ '\n'.join(coltab)+'\nAll four domains and every planned static point are retained. Divergent retrieval quality and cost behavior across model families is evidence against treating one retriever-specific frontier as a universal routing result. These exposed Dev measurements do not constitute a new independent test. Model loading, index construction, memory, query encoding and scoring are archived separately; unmeasured setup GPU fields remain missing.\n\n'
